{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448741-effects-of-other-metals","id":1448741,"title":"Effects of Other Metals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-16T19:12:40-07:00","id":1448741,"title":"Effects of Other Metals","content":"We know Silver and Gold are key weaknesses to the Changing Breeds as a whole, just as Iron is to the Fair Folk, but, what of other metals, Bronze? Copper? Platinum?<br /> <br /> one Concept I had was that Platinum could be like the reverse of Gold and Silver, holding it gives you a boost to Gnosis and healing, but inherently reduces raw attack strength in some manner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T19:28:32-07:00","id":1448742,"title":"","content":"That would make it broken like red paint in the Gundam franchise. Not something that you could probably do in a serious game, and it clashes against the &quot;can't sell what's important over the counter&quot; message, since anything that aids the Garou and Fera typically requires more work than even refining metal, or at least, a different, more personal kind of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T19:45:11-07:00","id":1448744,"title":"","content":"you raise a Valid point, but still, I want Platinum to have some sort of use that makes sense, especially as I have plans for stuff in the amazon, dealing with stuff that was once firmly in the grip of Meso-American Fera Tribes and Factions, and that region is well known as a Platinum Hot zone, contrasting how Europe was such a dead zone for it that colonists didn't even recognize it for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T20:20:00-07:00","id":1448747,"title":"","content":"Gold and silver, thematically, aren't banes to the Changing Breeds because they're themed after metals. They're banes because they're themed after <i>celestial patrons,</i> precious materials symbolic of the Sun and Moon. It doesn't matter how strong or rare or valuable a metal is, it matters whether it holds totemic resonance with one of the great Celestines who has invested their power in their favored children.<br /> <br /> The traditional planetary metals of Western alchemy, incidentally, are mercury for Mercury, copper for Venus, iron for Mars, tin for Jupiter, and lead for Saturn, in addition to the above gold and silver. Platinum falls with the secondary metals as a less pure derivation from the planetary metals and is written with a combination of Sun and Moon, but is presumably not as directly spriritually resonant with either as actual gold or silver.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder about the faeries and Mars, if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T20:39:13-07:00","id":1448748,"title":"","content":"I have always pondered how the Garou and Fera would handle a future setting where space travel and terraforming of planets in the solar system started being the norm, and how it might impact the spirit umbra of such places and their Celestine patrons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T22:27:02-07:00","id":1448753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448741-effects-of-other-metals?p=1448747#post1448747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The traditional planetary metals of Western alchemy, incidentally, are mercury for Mercury, copper for Venus, iron for Mars, tin for Jupiter, and lead for Saturn, in addition to the above gold and silver. Platinum falls with the secondary metals as a less pure derivation from the planetary metals and is written with a combination of Sun and Moon, but is presumably not as directly spriritually resonant with either as actual gold or silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I could remember where I read the suggestion that Neptune, discovered in 1848, should be associated with technology and Aluminum, while Pluto, from 1930, would be associated with genocide and Uranium or Plutonium. I think Uranus (1781) was suggested as revolution, but I can't recall what metal was suggested. (Obviously conventional astrology has its own associations and alchemical symbols for them, but I always found those suggestions interesting.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T22:53:11-07:00","id":1448754,"title":"","content":"The 1e PG had a whole write up on speciallized herbalism, KOTE companion has a whole write up on specially awakened Jade. So I can see SOMTHING working from various metals even ifs no a one for one. Maybe rites that properly align them to their celestial patron might give some bonuses here and there... like specialized Talens...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T23:42:01-07:00","id":1448756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448741-effects-of-other-metals?p=1448747#post1448747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gold and silver, thematically, aren't banes to the Changing Breeds because they're themed after metals. They're banes because they're themed after <i>celestial patrons,</i> precious materials symbolic of the Sun and Moon. It doesn't matter how strong or rare or valuable a metal is, it matters whether it holds totemic resonance with one of the great Celestines who has invested their power in their favored children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Silver is consider the lunar metal as gold is the solar metal. The game never explains why they would hurt the Changing Breeds, but the reason I give my players is that they are essentially a Ban from their celestial patron. Luna blesses the Garou, so in return all Garou have the ban that the lunar metal hurts them. Likewise for Helios and the Breeds closer to him. That's just how the magic works. You can't have the benefit without accepting the Ban.<br /> <br /> However, there are other metals or materials that do have magical associations as well.<br /> <br /> Mercury is also known as quicksilver, and in some lore harms werewolves just as silver does. And while mercury is liquid at normal temperatures, it can become solid as an amalgam with most other metals. It's been universally considered a very magical metal with lots of properties.<br /> <br /> Iron was associated with magic because the skill needed to forge weapons and items from it was extremely high. A smith needed to know a lot of &quot;secrets&quot; to make useful iron/steel items that was not needed to make bronze items. And the ubiquity of iron, compared to copper and tin, meant far more people could have metal tools and weapons. It proved so useful in allowing mankind to master its environment, it is not a surprise people associated it with all sorts of protective properties. Although modern werewolf lore and the game does not ascribe any properties to it for use against werewolves, there are somey folktales about how throwing a piece of iron over a werewolf's head (often a knife, but it could be another item) would transform it back into a person.<br /> <br /> Outside of metals, salt was also a material with very strong magical properties. The connection between salt and life is very strong, and thus was often seen as a defense against all sorts of supernatural evil. It should have some kind of role in the game.<br /> <br /> Even an ST doesn't want the physical metal or material itself to have supernatural effects, I do think that spirits of metal should have Charms or properties that evoke them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T00:39:37-07:00","id":1448757,"title":"","content":"Well, the association with celestial bodies surely is tied to them being rare and valuable metals and vice versa.<br /> Also, the use as weaponry has to make some sense, thematically.<br /> Sunflowers also represent the sun, to some degree, yet you can't to unsoakable damage to a Mokol\u00e9 by stabbing him with a sunflower's stalk.<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;Ban&quot; explanation works well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}